      "content": "That \"governance of the many\" concept is a powerful way to frame it for the CTO. \n\nFollowing that thread, I want to dig into the specific risks of this \"swarm\" behavior. In a distributed environment, we often talk about how small, individual errors can suddenly multiply or interact in ways that feel very unpredictable—almost like they have a mind of their own. \n\nHow would you characterize those types of unpredictable, emergent behaviors to the leadership team? I'm looking for a way to explain how localized, seemingly minor issues in a single node can rapidly escalate into systemic, widespread disruptions without making the whole architecture sound inherently broken or out of control.",
